she is lovely yes but so young  season four of the crown has been the  most controversial yet  with creator peter morgan admitting that  some of the stories depicted stray away  from the truth  the past three seasons have stayed quite  true to history so let's have a look at  what they depicted honestly and where  they skewed away from the facts this  time around  this season depicts prince charles  finding diana dressed as a shrub from a  school production of shakespeare's a  midsummer night's dream  this is a complete disaster as cute as  this was  the truth is they were actually  introduced at a party at althorp estate  by diana's older sister sarah  they then met again at a house in sussex  and after that they began dating  leading to their engagement in 1981.  in the crown they show diana choosing  her engagement ring from a selection of  many beautiful pieces  this one's lovely this is quite accurate  diana did choose the gorgeous diamonds  and sapphires that made her legendary  ring  however the location wasn't so accurate  the show had diana picking out her ring  at bergly house  when really she made the decision at  windsor castle in real life  the engagement ring was given to her son  prince harry after the princess  tragically passed away  he then passed it on to his brother  prince william to propose to kate  middleton with  the queen has some of the top security  in the world  so it comes as quite the shock to see a  strange man breaking into the queen's  bedroom during the fifth episode  in the queen's bedroom in the middle of  the night the show was right about this  a man named michael fagan did in fact  manage to break into buckingham palace  and surprise the queen in her room  fagin had actually managed to make his  way past the high security and into the  palace  twice on the second occasion making it  all the way to the queen  what the crown got wrong was the  10-minute conversation they depicted  between the two  what your toothbrush in reality  the queen was understandably shocked and  scurried out of her room to find help  this did actually happen and as  mentioned before  sarah is the one who introduced diana to  prince charles the two dated in 1977  when sarah was 22 and the prince was 28.  it wasn't quite the best match though as  lady sarah said that while she enjoyed  dating the prince  she never imagined marrying him ouch  this season portrays prince charles  receiving a harsh letter from his great  uncle  lord louis mountbatten in the letter he  writes that he is a shame and  disappointment to the family for  continuing to entertain the idea of a  relationship with camilla parker-bowles  who was married at the time there is no  evidence to prove that this letter ever  existed  and the show's creator peter morgan has  admitted to the fact that he made up  this detail  his defense for the falsity is that he  believes that's how lord louis  mountbatten felt and that he could have  written a letter saying the same things  in a scandalous moment in episode 3.  princess diana stumbles upon a design of  a bracelet with the letters  g and f engraved on it this  is mostly true except in reality diana  found an actual bracelet  not just a design with the same  engraving this is wildly upsetting to  diana as before this  camilla explained to her that she and  prince charles called each other  gladys and fred the crown did stray away  from the truth a bit here  as kimila was never actually the one to  tell diana about the nicknames  the princess found out through prince  charles's friends and a note she once  discovered  right further it is not confirmed that  their nicknames for each other were fred  and gladys  according to author jonathan dimbleby  the letters g  and f actually stood for girl friday a  nickname prince charles had for camilla  this season portrays a very tense  relationship between the queen and the  prime minister margaret thatcher  oh is that while it made for some juicy  scenes  this just wasn't the case first off  according to a biography on queen  elizabeth written by sally bettle smith  the queen did not offer advice or  opinions to the pm  and did not get involved with political  parties secondly the two women actually  had quite a bit in common they both had  a strong sense of their christian faith  grew up during the war and had a strong  sense of duty to their country  while there were reports of friction  between the two margaret thatcher  confirmed in her autobiography that this  was false did princess diana and her  father-in-law prince philip actually go  hunting together at balmoral  the answer is no however the  relationship depicted between the two on  the show is quite accurate  the princess and prince did have a very  cordial relationship  when princess die and prince charles  were struggling during their marriage  prince philip went so far as to write  diana letters in support of her  episode 3 has princess margaret speaking  out against the upcoming wedding of  prince charles and lady die  but he's still in love with the other  one suggesting it should not go ahead  this is entirely false and has been  confirmed by the actress herself  helena bonham carter has explained that  it was her idea to include that in the  season  since season one shared the story of the  downfall of the relationship between  princess margaret and peter townsend  due to interference from the royal  family we can understand why the  princess may have felt some resentment  however the idea that she tried to stop  the marriage holds no truth  another defamatory claim in this season  is that upon returning from a trip to  new zealand australia and the us  prince charles went straight to  highgrove to be with camilla  this never could have actually happened  as when he returned from the trip  highgrove was being renovated  because  i love you prince charles and princess  diana only moved to highgrove in late  1981.  sadly the princess did battle an eating  disorder for a decade  much to the chagrin of the royal family  she even spoke out about it publicly and  said that the bulimia was a symptom of  her marriage to prince charles  episode 9 depicts a wild scene in which  princess die  slips away from prince charles while  attending a show at the royal opera  house and shortly after  appears on stage in a silk negligee  dancing to billy joel's hit  uptown girl unbelievable as this may  seem  it's entirely true in both the show in  real life  prince charles was deeply unimpressed  with this surprise  there were six days that the son of the  prime minister did go missing in the  sahara desert while in the paris dakar  rally  but the crown didn't get right was their  timing the show has her son mark  thatcher  going missing around the same time as  the falklands war the war began in april  1982  whereas mark went missing in january  1982  another dramatic moment this season had  prince charles being caught in an  avalanche and losing his dear friend  major hugh lindsey as a result  tragically  this was a real event the prince of  wales is safe  prince charles was saved from the  avalanche by helicopter but it was still  a very close call  the two royals did in fact embark on a  tour of australia  including a stop in perth the way the  show had diana dressed was very accurate  to the occasion as well  what the show didn't get right was who  actually made the appearance in perth  the fact is this event actually marked  princess dye's first solo public  appearance  the crown depicts both prince charles  and the princess appearing  with the majority of the attention on  diana instead of being left in the  background  the prince was never really there at all  at the end of the day  it's hard to know what is truth and what  is fiction since none of us were  actually there to see for ourselves  what we do know for sure is that the  queen's communication secretary has said  that  the royal household has never agreed to  vet or approve content  has not asked to know what topics will  be included and would never express a  view as to the program's accuracy  now we're wondering how factual seasons  five and six will be since they strayed  so far this time around  do you prefer the historical facts or  the story netflix is sharing  let us know in the comments below don't  forget to hit that subscribe button and  give us a like if you enjoyed this video  you
 

